ment of eating disorders, affecting patients' mental health and coping mechanisms.", "DINÁMICA FAMILIAR:Family dynamics can significantly impact the psychological well-being of patients with eating disorders, often contributing to their condition.", "PSICOTERAPIA:PSICOTERAPIA es un tratamiento que implica la interacción entre un paciente y un terapeuta, utilizado para abordar trastornos psicológicos, incluyendo los trastornos de la conducta alimentaria. Este enfoque terapéutico es fundamental en el tratamiento de los trastornos alimentarios, ya que se centra en tratar los problemas psicológicos subyacentes y fomentar la recuperación del paciente.", "VALORACIÓN INICIAL:Initial assessment for patients with eating disorders includes various tests such as hemogram, glucose levels, and renal function tests.", "PRUEBAS A CONSIDERAR:Subsequent tests for evaluating patients with eating disorders may include serum iron, hormonal levels, and gastrointestinal studies.", "MANIFESTACIONES CLÍNICAS:Clinical manifestations of eating disorders are multisystemic due to malnutrition, affecting almost all parts of the body and potentially causing irreversible damage.", "ALTERACIONES CARDIOVASCULARES:Cardiovascular alterations in patients with anorexia nerviosa include bradycardia, hypotension, and various electrocardiographic abnormalities.", "ALTERACIONES DIGESTIVAS:ALTERACIONES DIGESTIVAS refer to a range of digestive issues commonly associated with anorexia nerviosa. These alterations include decreased gastrointestinal motility and delayed gastric emptying, which can significantly impact the digestive process. Additionally, these digestive disorders can affect nutrient absorption, potentially necessitating the use of enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake.", "GASTROPARESIA:Gastroparesis is a medical condition that affects the stomach muscles, preventing proper stomach emptying. It is often observed in diabetic patients and can lead to significant weight loss, particularly in cases such as anorexia nervosa. The condition is characterized by delayed gastric emptying, which can result in increased gastric residue, especially in patients receiving enteral nutrition. Improvement in gastroparesis symptoms is typically achieved through nutritional rehabilitation and dietary adjustments.", "PROTEÍNAS VISCERALES:Visceral proteins are evaluated in the initial assessment to assess nutritional status and liver function in patients with eating disorders."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}